      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=2,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X-5].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X-5] & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
